        "date": "2026-11-09T01:02:00Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): machine files for the PCNC 770 and PCNC 1100 from their manuals\n\nFour inch machine files, each built from the Specifications section of\nits own Tormach operator's manual:\n\n- Tormach PCNC 770 (Series 3): 32426 Rev C1-1. Rapids are 135/100 IPM.\n  The earlier B1-4 manual says 130 IPM for X/Y, and the later revision\n  wins.\n- Tormach PCNC 1100 (Series I): 30625 Rev C4-1, 300-4500 rpm, 65 IPM.\n- Tormach PCNC 1100 (Series II): 31138 Rev B1-4, 100-5140 rpm, 90/65 IPM.\n- Tormach PCNC 1100 (Series 3): UM10087 1013A, 100-5140 rpm, 110/90 IPM.\n\nEach file states both belt ranges and the rated motor power (not the\npeak), plus Flood M8 and Mist M7. Each also sets rigid_tapping false:\nthese are R8 mills that tap with the M871-M874 tapping-head macros, so\nthe Tormach post refuses a G84 on them by name.\n\nAll four are registered in posting::MACHINES and pinned in\ntests/machine.rs and tests/tormach_machines.rs (figures, belt notes,\ntap refusal). Sources, pages and the 770 disagreement are recorded in\ndocs/decisions/170-tormach-pcnc.md.\n\nRefs #170\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
