      "message": "feat(post): machine files for the Tormach 1100M and PCNC 770 from their manuals\n\nTwo more inch machine files, each from its own Tormach operator's\nmanual:\n\n- Tormach 1100M (PathPilot era): UM10540 0626A, sections 2.1-2.2\n  (pp. 32-33). Travel 18 x 11 x 16.25 in, 70-7500 rpm on two Poly-V\n  belt ranges (70-2000 / 250-7500), 2 hp (1.5 kW), 110/90 IPM, R8.\n  rigid_tapping is false. The spec sheet lists thread machining as\n  \"Tension/Compression, Auto-Reversing, Thread Mill\", the 770M's line,\n  so the Tormach post refuses a G84 on it by name. The manual states\n  no ATC pocket count and never mentions the 1100M+, so no 1100M+ file\n  is made.\n- Tormach PCNC 770 (before Series 3): 31725 Rev B1-4, section 9.4.1\n  (PDF p. 142), every figure re-read from B1-4 itself. It is the\n  Series 3's iron with a 130 IPM X/Y rapid (Series 3: 135).\n\nBoth are registered in posting::MACHINES and pinned in tests/machine.rs\nand tests/tormach_machines.rs (figures, belt notes, tap refusal), and\nlisted in the README. Sources and pages are in\ndocs/decisions/170-tormach-pcnc.md.\n\nEvery model in #170's title (1500MX, 1100MX, 1100, 770, 770M, PCNC 440)\nand the 1100M now has a file.\n\nFixes #170\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
